# <PROJECT NAME> — Tabouleh Rules

This project uses Tabouleh, attached at `<TABOULEH_PATH>` (e.g.
`./tabouleh` via symlink or submodule). These rules apply to all work in
this project regardless of which phase (see Workflow below) is active.

## Kitchen Rules (non-negotiable)

Full source of truth: `<TABOULEH_PATH>/core/KITCHEN_RULES.md` — read it,
don't rely only on this summary. Every action falls into one of three
responses:

- **CONFIRM** — stop, state exactly what will happen, get an explicit yes
  before doing it.
- **BLOCK** — never do this, no confirmation unlocks it; explain why and
  propose an alternative, or escalate.
- **Unrestricted** — normal work, no gate.

Gated categories include: force-push / history-rewriting git operations on
shared branches, deletions outside the current Ticket's own scratch files,
dependency additions/removals, database migrations run against anything
but a local database, anything touching secrets/credentials, and anything
touching production or real user data. See the source file for the
complete, specific list — this file does not override or weaken it.

## Workflow (The Pass)

Full source of truth: `<TABOULEH_PATH>/core/THE_PASS.md`. Work moves
through five phases: **Ticket** (planned and approved before code is
written) → **Fire** (implement) → **Plate** (self-review) → **Expedite**
(independent check against the Ticket) → **Serve** (done).

Because Cursor doesn't separate roles the way Claude Code's `.claude/agents/`
does, announce which phase is active and self-enforce its boundaries:

- In **Ticket**, only produce the Ticket document — no code edits.
- In **Fire**, only touch files listed in the Ticket's Files Touched.
- In **Plate**, run the self-review checklist in
  `<TABOULEH_PATH>/core/recipes/recipe-self-review.md` before declaring
  work ready for Expedite.
- In **Expedite**, treat this as read-only: check the diff against the
  Ticket's acceptance criteria and report findings, do not edit files
  during this phase even though nothing prevents it mechanically.

Tickets are created under `<TICKETS_PATH>` (e.g. `./tickets/`) using
`<TABOULEH_PATH>/core/templates/ticket.template.md`.

